{"request_sha256": "ae302308332b5be5bd22aa31ae428595bb1c0c58ca5b4f142ad3d48e6d0b49b9", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "e53d0b233227ae12ca5629fa902632fb91824c9f08f89dfe05fe0cafd3c8cc50", "schema_sha256": "40b44f74e2832e0e52874cb964ff3f11b714cc6333ecca85f93378397c38d7cc", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 4, "output_tokens": 12485}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail"], "defects": ["crown-dense-ovoid-to-conic: render-0 crown is airy and see-through — continuous sky gaps and long bare interior limbs are visible through the upper two-thirds, and foliage sits in separated clumps rather than one continuous mass; reference-0 shows an opaque, bumpy, cauliflower-surfaced crown. Defining mismatch of a core trait.", "branch-layered-horizontal-tiers: render-0 upper and mid crown is a radial fan of long, straight, steeply ascending limbs from one low fork, with foliage carried near the tips; the near-horizontal stacked tiers with slightly down-arching tips seen in reference-0 and reference-1 are confined to the lowest limbs. Defining mismatch of a core trait.", "bole-short-with-basal-flare: the short-bole half is supported, but the flare half is not — in render-0 the visible trunk meets the ground plane as a near-straight column with only slight widening and no broad low root swellings, whereas reference-0 and reference-1 show a smooth buttressed base spreading into the lawn.", "winter-fine-twiggy-periphery (core) is unassessable: no leafless render was supplied for this identity, so the core winter-periphery trait carried by reference-1 has no render counterpart. Required-unknown, not a dismissal.", "bark-lichen-flecking (core) is unassessable at the supplied scale: the render-0 bole is plain pale grey with no resolvable flecking, but whole-view framing gives it too few pixels to decide presence or absence against the reference-2 close-up."], "observations": ["The required set is a single cell: reference_character at view B-WHOLE, judged from render-0 against reference-0/1/2 jointly, with anchor-0 used for finish/style only.", "render-0 shows a solitary leafed broadleaf on a flat ground plane: crown taller than wide, pale whitish-grey smooth unfissured bole forking low into many ascending limbs, foliage in discrete granular clumps with abundant visible interior structure and sky.", "reference-1 and reference-2 are the same image file and checksum under two view labels; the bare-crown panel and the bark close-up sit side by side in that one frame, so the bare and bark evidence is not independent.", "No claim is made or assumed that any reference frame shows the same specimen as another, nor that any difference between frames reflects change over time.", "Reference backgrounds (building, fence, playground, benches) are context only and were not used as morphology evidence.", "Ranked largest grounded gaps: (1) crown density/opacity, (2) upper-crown branch architecture (radial fan vs horizontal tiers), (3) absent basal flare, (4) trunk tone markedly paler with flecking unresolvable, (5) foliage spray organisation reading sparse rather than densely shingled.", "Finish quality relative to anchor-0 is adequate for the catalogue finish floor (coherent shading, soft ground shadow, consistent material response); the failures recorded here are morphological, not finish-level, and no photorealism or pixel-matching standard was applied.", "Improvement relative to earlier rounds was not considered; readiness is judged absolutely against the frozen inventory."], "findings": [{"observation": "render-0 crown interior is open: sky shows through the upper two-thirds in many places and long unclothed limbs read as distinct sticks against the foliage. reference-0's left panel is fully opaque through the upper crown and its right panel shows only small lower/mid gaps; render-0 exceeds that band.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Possibly insufficient leaf density or foliage placed too distally on long internodes; mechanism not established from the image."}, {"observation": "In render-0 the dominant pattern above the fork is a radial spray of long straight ascending limbs; the near-horizontal layered tiers with slightly down-arching tips, present in both reference-0 and the reference-1 bare panel, appear only in the lowest limbs.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Could follow from branch-angle or gravimorphism settings; not determinable from a single view."}, {"observation": "render-0's bole is short before forking, matching the reference habit, but the base meets the ground as a near-straight column with only slight widening and no broad root swellings, unlike the smooth buttressed flare in reference-0 and reference-1.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "No leafless render exists for this identity, so the core fine-twiggy winter periphery described from reference-1 has no counterpart to compare against.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "render-0's trunk is smooth and unfissured over its full visible height with no ridges, plates or peeling, consistent with the reference bark relief, though the tone is notably paler and whiter than the mid-grey of reference-2.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Pale whitish bark flecking is not resolvable on the render-0 bole at whole-view scale; absence cannot be distinguished from scale limitation, so no conclusion is drawn either way.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "render-0 crown height clearly exceeds crown width, within the range spanned by the two reference-0 panels (taller-than-wide left, near-equal right).", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "render-0's lowest limbs sweep outward and downward to well below mid-height, leaving only a short clear bole beneath the skirt, consistent with the low-skirted habit in reference-0.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Foliage colour in render-0 is mid to deep green with lighter sun-facing outer zones and shaded interiors and no marked blue or grey cast, matching reference-0; the mild sheen difference is acceptable variation.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "render-0 depicts an open-grown solitary specimen with unrestricted lateral room, the same expression represented in all references; the forest-grown narrow form is not in evidence on either side.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Leaf granularity in render-0 suggests small simple leaves, but they read as separated clumps rather than overlapping flat sprays along branchlets; individual leaves are unresolvable on both sides, so spray organisation cannot be settled.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "A deeper trunk tone, faint vertical streaking and a slightly glossier leaf sheen would move render-0 closer to the references but are refinement, not defining character.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Finish and style of render-0 sit at or above the established catalogue anchor level; the anchor is a different species and was used for finish only, contributing nothing to the morphology verdict.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "anchor-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "bark-smooth-unfissured-grey", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Render bole is smooth, unfissured, matte and columnar over its full visible height with no ridges, plates or peeling, matching the reference bark relief; the paler tone is recorded as refinement, not a defining break."}, {"trait_id": "bark-lichen-flecking", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Reference evidence is a bark close-up; the render supplies only a whole-view bole at which flecks of the stated apparent scale would not resolve. Neither presence nor absence is supported."}, {"trait_id": "crown-dense-ovoid-to-conic", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Outline is broadly ovoid, but density is contradicted: continuous sky gaps and bare interior limbs run through the upper two-thirds of the render crown, where reference-0 shows an opaque bumpy mass."}, {"trait_id": "crown-tall-relative-to-spread", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Render crown height clearly exceeds width, inside the range spanned by the two reference-0 panels."}, {"trait_id": "foliage-to-low-skirt", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Lowest limbs sweep out and down to well below mid-height, leaving only a short clear bole, as in reference-0."}, {"trait_id": "branch-layered-horizontal-tiers", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The render's upper and mid crown is a radial fan of steeply ascending straight limbs; the near-horizontal stacked tiers with down-arching tips seen in both references are confined to the lowest limbs."}, {"trait_id": "bole-short-with-basal-flare", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The short stout bole dividing into several scaffolds is supported, but the visible base is an essentially straight column without the smooth buttressed flare and low root swellings the references show."}, {"trait_id": "winter-fine-twiggy-periphery", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "No leafless render was supplied; the leafed frame cannot resolve periphery twig fineness. Core trait left explicitly unknown rather than dismissed."}, {"trait_id": "winter-branch-hierarchy", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary trait; no bare-silhouette render exists for this identity, and the leafed render occludes the scaffold-to-twig size progression."}, {"trait_id": "foliage-mid-green-glossy", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Mid to deep green with lit outer highlights and dark interiors, no blue or grey cast; sheen difference is acceptable variation."}, {"trait_id": "leaf-small-dense-shingled", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Leaves are unresolvable in both render and reference; render granularity suggests small leaves but in separated clumps, which is not enough to confirm or refute flat shingled sprays."}, {"trait_id": "leaf-margin-venation", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Below resolution in every supplied frame on both sides; the inventory itself records no evidence."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-dark-vertical-streaking", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary trait; the render bole shows a few faint dark marks near the fork, but whole-view scale cannot establish presence or absence of the streaking pattern."}, {"trait_id": "crown-interior-visible-limbs", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Declared a variation band, but the render sits outside it: interior limbs and sky are visible throughout the upper crown, beyond the lower/mid-crown gaps of the more open reference-0 panel. Recorded as a contributor to the crown-density blocker."}, {"trait_id": "habit-open-grown-context", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Render presents an open-grown solitary specimen with free lateral room, the same expression the references represent."}, {"trait_id": "reference-view-redundancy", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Inventory-level observation about the evidence set, not a render property: reference-1 and reference-2 share one file and checksum, and whether any two references depict the same individual is not determinable."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"514c9dd2-29ce-4423-9958-b1f5e9baff7f","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_servers":[],"model":"claude-opus-5","permissionMode":"default","slash_commands":["deep-research","design","design-sync","dataviz","update-config","verify","debug","code-review","simplify","batch","fewer-permission-prompts","doctor","loop","schedule","claude-api","workflow-authoring","run","run-skill-generator","advisor","agents","auto-mode-setup","autocompact","clear","color","compact","config","output-style","context","effort","fast","heapdump","init","mcp","import","model","__remote-workflow","wo